        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="plugL348IgNCwrQeIHvL-88" parent="plugL348IgNCwrQeIHvL-48" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="35" width="39.11" x="61" y="37.5" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="plugL348IgNCwrQeIHvL-90" parent="plugL348IgNCwrQeIHvL-48" style="shape=image;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=default;verticalAlign=top;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/png,;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="20" width="20" x="71" y="45" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="plugL348IgNCwrQeIHvL-84" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 27px;&quot;&gt;Startup mode&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 13px;&quot;&gt;When a user starts up the application, this will be the first window they see. It has a minimal setup to switch between all possible modes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 13px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 13px;&quot;&gt;The &#39;Run&#39; button goes straight to the &#39;Running&#39; mode. When a user clicks it, two side effects may occur: immediate run or a file dialog. Immediate run happens when the &#39;Default PID&#39; is set otherwise a modal file dialog with running processes opens up. To set the &#39;Default PID&#39;, a user must switch to the &#39;Settings&#39; mode. Once a process id is defined, the application switches its mode to &#39;Running&#39;.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 13px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 13px;&quot;&gt;The question mark &#39;?&#39; button on the right corner switches to the &#39;Information&#39; mode. It has a conditional look depending on the current mode a user is in. In this case it will open a new modal window with a text explaining how to use the application similar to this description.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 13px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 13px;&quot;&gt;The &#39;Logs&#39;&amp;nbsp; shows all the interactions a user has made. There are three possible logs: errors, warnings and notes. Things like mode switchings and settings setups are considered notes. A user can extend the log bar to get more logs.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 13px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 13px;&quot;&gt;The &#39;Settings&#39; button sits on the top-left corner. It switches the mode to &#39;Settings&#39; immediately and logs it.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="400" width="760" x="40" y="320" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="plugL348IgNCwrQeIHvL-85" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;Settings mode&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;This mode contains all the configurations a user can make for the application runtime.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The arrow button takes place of the &#39;Settings&#39; button from the &#39;Startup&#39; mode. By clicking it, a user returns to the mode they were previously in.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The question mark button opens up a modal window where it provides a small article explaining how to use this mode and what each settings is responsible for.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The &#39;Logs&#39; block contains all the application logs including all the changes a user made throughout the runtime. It can be extended to get more logs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The settings are defined in the top-center. For now, there are two possible settings types:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;1) Server File Path -- a path to the executable server program. By default it&#39;s undefined and it should be set manually&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; 2) Default PID -- a process id that needs to be monitored. By default it&#39;s &#39;null&#39; and when switching to the &#39;Running&#39; mode a user will be prompted to choose a currently available running process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="380" width="760" x="37.89" y="1030" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="plugL348IgNCwrQeIHvL-87" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;Running Mode&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;The &#39;Running&#39; mode is open once a process is selected after clicking the &#39;Run&#39; button. The frontend instantiates a new server process and connects to it. In case of connection failures the &#39;Logs&#39; is populated with corresponding messages.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The initial design is composed of a &#39;Usage bar&#39; that shows how much CPU resources are being allocated at a given time. It also has a block of thread metrics. Basically a graph where every thread is assigned its position.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Similarly to other modes, there is a &#39;Settings&#39; button to switch to the &#39;Settings&#39; mode and the question mark button to go the &#39;About&#39; mode.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;There is also a stop/resume button next to the &#39;Settings&#39; one for letting the server check the metrics or not.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="480" width="760" x="40" y="1720" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
